aspectRatio",1.7777777777777777,"mobile","previewSrc","Preview description","Official SolarWM overview title over a grid of generated environments with movement controls","alt","Recording type","Original project recording","role","provenance","Track","World models","track","metadata","Related project",[91],"resourceId",{"_49":92,"_26":93},"SolarWM","/resources/solarwm/","What this recording shows","A recorded world-model overview, not an interactive browser game. Some sequences are sped up, as stated in the video. The preview does not establish editable geometry, persistent entity rules, or gameplay logic.","limitations","Demo category","World model","demoType","lead","world","world-model","source-recording","recordingId","solarwm","resource:solarwm","resource","An interactive video world model framework for open data, training, and long-horizon inference.","/resources/",{"_20":105,"_186":92,"_184":101,"_47":187,"_185":108,"_180":179,"_26":177,"_57":188,"_155":189,"_150":190,"_146":191,"_140":192,"_137":136},[113,114,115,116,117,118,119,120,121,122,123,124,125,126],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_47":22,"_51":92,"_53":186,"_55":-7},{"_47":100,"_51":108,"_53":185,"_55":-7},{"_47":48,"_49":183,"_51":85,"_53":184,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_49":181,"_51":182,"_53":47,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_49":178,"_51":179,"_53":180,"_55":56},{"_47":57,"_49":174,"_59":175,"_53":26,"_55":-7},{"_47":57,"_49":161,"_59":162,"_53":57,"_55":-7},{"_47":141,"_49":153,"_143":144,"_59":154,"_53":155,"_55":-7},{"_47":141,"_49":148,"_143":144,"_59":149,"_53":150,"_55":-7},{"_47":141,"_49":142,"_143":144,"_59":145,"_53":146,"_55":-7},{"_47":48,"_49":138,"_51":139,"_53":140,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_49":135,"_51":136,"_53":137,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_53":132,"_49":133,"_51":134},{"_47":57,"_53":127,"_49":128,"_59":129},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[130],{"_49":131,"_26":63},"The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen","identity","Identity & attribution","First author Junchao Huang is affiliated with CUHK-SZ and SLAI. Select the first listed institution, CUHK-Shenzhen, not the separate CUHK campus. The project also lists NUS, CUHK, HKUST, HKUST-GZ, NVIDIA, UCLA, and MSRA. The logo is the Home image in the official CUHK-Shenzhen homepage HTML.","Source reviewed","2026-10-19","verified","Year","2026","year","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[147,85],"dimensions","3D","Development stages",[151,152,85],"stages","Gameplay & code","Engines & scenes","Topics",[156,157,158,159,160],"tags","interactive-video","training-framework","camera-control","streaming","released-code","Further reading",[163,164,165,166],{"_49":172,"_26":173},{"_49":171,"_26":63},{"_49":169,"_26":170},{"_49":167,"_26":168},"H3 weights and access","https://huggingface.co/junchaoh-cs/SolarWM-H3-33B","Data access","https://huggingface.co/datasets/junchaoh-cs/SolarWM-Data","Project","Code and documentation","https://github.com/Junchao-cs/SolarWM","Project source",[176],{"_49":174,"_26":177},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.02886","Why it belongs here","Unifies data, training, and inference interfaces for camera-controlled streaming video. The source matrix lists all three stages for Wan2.2-5B and MiniMax-H3, but later stages for Wan2.2-14B and LTX-2.5 remain forthcoming. Backbones require separate runtime environments. The main data release contains annotations and indexes; latent payloads are separate, and the full processed training-video corpus requires reconstruction or approved access. The main Hugging Face dataset and H3 model repositories also require agreement to share contact information. This infrastructure does not provide a code world with queryable entity state.","detail","Resource type","Paper","Category","category","summary","name","paper",[196,197,198,199],[156,157,158,159,160],[194,195,101],[193,101],2026,"3d","code","scene",{"_49":172,"_26":173},{"_49":171,"_26":63},{"_49":169,"_26":170},{"_49":167,"_26":168},{"_201":202},"documents",{"_203":204,"_205":206},"en",[208,212,213,214,211,215,